# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the tsan test preset.
#
# Only races inside system libraries belong here, never bdex code: each
# entry names a library the engine does not control and says why.

# OpenAL Soft and the PipeWire backend it uses on Linux desktops sync their
# mixing threads with atomics and lock-free ring buffers in code TSan does
# not instrument, so it reports their hand-offs as races. The engine only
# calls OpenAL from its streaming thread, which OpenAL Soft allows (the
# context is current process-wide). CI machines have no audio device.
race:libopenal.so
race:libpipewire
race:libspa
